        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <p>
        <strong>Business Scheduling Example:</strong> A software developer in St. John's (NDT, UTC-2:30) hosting a training webinar for a client in Vancouver (PDT, UTC-7) must coordinate across a 4.5-hour difference. 
        To hold the webinar at 10:00 AM PDT for the West Coast client, the developer must schedule it for 2:30 PM NDT local time.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Travel Example:</strong> Flying from St. John's (YYT) to Toronto (YYZ) takes about 3 hours. 
        Because Toronto is 1.5 hours behind St. John's, a traveler departing at 8:00 AM NST will land at 9:30 AM EST, making the flight feel exceptionally short.
      </p>
    </article>

